00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.829 align:start position:0%
 
thank you  good evening everyone uh welcome to this  meeting of the standards committee  especially to our newer members of the  committee i will now read out the  emergency evacuation announcement  should we be required to evacuate the  building would you please leave the  building via the entry doors to the  media block and continue straight on the  right hand side  of the car park where the assembly point  is  please do not delay your evacuation to  collect any belongings please do not  return to the building until given  permission to do so by council staff  please note that the meeting will be  audio recorded please switch off any  mobiles or turn them to xylem  members you will see microphones are  provided for you on the tables for use  during the meeting  when i invite you to speak please ensure  that there is a microphone in front of  you before speaking  as microphones are needed for the  hearing loop and for the audio recording  where possible please help by passing  microphones to each other and use the  hand gel and antibacterial wipes on the  tables if you do touch the microphones  members voting will be done on a show of  hands in line with constitution  i will ask for a show of hands for and  against  the recommendations and then for those  wishing to abstain from voting  so agenda item number one  tonight apologies for absence  um we have apologies from councillor  mrs mandy cohen has anybody else  any other apologies  no  thank you  we have no substitute members  gender item number three  agenda item number three non-members  attending we have no  other members attending apart from the  committee members but we do have a guest  we have mr steve summers who's the  strategic director  agenda item number four  minutes of the meeting held on the 29th  of march 2022.  um understandably this is more for those  members who were on the committee last  year are the minutes agreed members  agreed  thank you  gender item number five are there any  declarations of interest  there's none  um of course if any come up during the  course of the evening please just raise  your hand and say so gender item number  six  the new local government association  model code of conduct  members our monitoring officer angela  law will present this report  thank you chairman um this reports to  present to the committee the new local  government association moral code of  conduct  with the view to making a recommendation  to the council to adopt and replace the  council's existing code under part five  of our constitution  this new code of conduct comes following  a report made by the committee on  standards in public life  and  it was approved  back in may 2021 um various monitoring  officers up and down the country  have been in contact with lga clarifying  certain parts and i think at this stage  with the essex other essex monitoring  officers  we are at a stage where we are happy  with the final code the latest version  of the code to be adopted  most of the um  essex monitoring officers have either  adopted or are in the process of  adopting the code including brentwood  our strategic partner  i'm not going to read the report  verbatim members but i'm happy to take  any questions you may have  members are there any questions  counselor mr myers  having read the report and then read the  um local government ethics ethical  standards report  i say it describes the uh  um  code of conduct as a toothless tiger  is is it possible for the council to  bring its own sanctions in  no um that's governed by the localism  that so we we can't bring our own  sanctions in however however uh  recommendations and sanctions um  yeah is discussed with the relevant  group leaders to sit to see what's the  appropriate you know sanctions to be  placed where a councillor has been found  to be in breach but there's no  powers for myself or the council to say  remove anyone from a committee or or or  indeed um  suspend them as a member  expect the only thing you can ever be  removed for basically he's going to  prison for three months isn't it apart  from that well if you go to prison for  three months you'll no longer be a  counsellor  are there any other questions  members  right um well i've got a question  um  angela on page 6.10 which is uh page 4.6  of the new code  um he talks around bullying harassment  and discrimination um my question really  is um  how does this fit in if it does at all  with indirect bullying or harassment  um  i'll give an example many many of the  councillors here quite familiar with  social media and unfortunately  at times there are both harassment and  bullying not necessarily  by a counsellor  but on occasions  a derogative  post or message against the councillor  has actually been liked by another  councillor so would that be included as  indirect bullying or harassment and  would it be under the code  the answer is quite potentially  could be under the code any retweets any  liking of post where um it you know  brings the council's reputation or  indeed the group's reputation into  disrepute i mean that can all be caught  under the code but it really depends on  each  single case and how it and the context  of it all  so it's a potential yes thank you  has anybody any other questions  okay um  i'd like to say a few words on the new  code  so with the new code of conduct being  written in the first person  is hope the councillors will take a  stronger more personal approach to  ensure their actions meet those expected  of a councillor  it aims to build on the seven principles  of public life which we all know as the  nolan principles they are selflessness  integrity  objectivity accountability  openness  honesty and leadership  the new code  now includes the definition of respect  also the term bullying  is a new addition to the code i will  draw your attention to page 6.10 of the  report 4.6 of the new code of conduct  respect means politeness and courtesy in  behavior speech and the written word  debate and having different views are  all part of a healthy democracy as a  counselor you can express challenge  criticize and disagree with views ideas  opinions and policies  in a robust but civil manner  you should not however subject  individuals groups of people or  organizations to personal attack  then goes on under bullying  the code refers to the advisory  conciliation arbitation service acas  and characteristics of bullying as  offensive intimidating malicious or  insulting behavior  an abuse or misuse of power through  means that undermine humiliate  denigrate or injure the recipient  bullying might be a regular pattern of  behavior or one-off incident  it could happen face-to-face on social  media in emails or phone calls  happen in the workplace  or at work  social events and may not always be  obvious or noticed by others  of course in politics  many may come from polar positions in  life  being respectful to each other can close  divisions it can enhance cooperation and  build collaboration  each and every councillor should be able  to undertake their role  without fear of being bullied or  ridiculed  in essence  through mutual politeness respect and  kindness  we will aid debate  listen better to each other and work  more collaboratively to serve our  residents  with this in mind  i would like to add a further  recommendation  that leaders of all parties collectively  pledge to uphold the new code of conduct  within their parties and members  in addition to encourage any candidates  and campaigners to embrace the nolan  principles  do i have a  secondary i'd like to second that please  thank you councillor  mike wilkinson his second bet  yep may we have a vote in that please  members  if you're in favor please raise your  hand  so  to that  further recommendation  and i will repeat it again  the leaders of all parties collectively  pledge to uphold the new code of conduct  within their parties and members  in addition to encourage any candidates  and campaigners to embrace the nolan  principles  those in favor is  those against please members  and those abstaining  one  thank you  gentlemen  um  so members there is uh now  the recommendation that is on  paragraph 9.1 on page 6.5 of the report  that the  council adopts the ldga model code of  conduct  with effect from first of august 2022 a  set out in appendix one  and the additional  recommendation  that leaders of all parties collectively  pledge to uphold the new code of conduct  within their parties and members  in addition to encourage any candidates  and campaigners to embrace the nolan  principles may we take those on block  members  if you'd like to vote in favor  for  those against  none those abstaining please  that is carrie thank you very much  members  and the meeting  is now closed at 1943.  thank you very much for coming out this  evening members thank you

